# Citation metadata for this repository.
#
# INCOMPLETE ON PURPOSE. Every field below is either verifiable from the
# repository itself (git history, the remote, pyproject.toml) or marked as a
# placeholder for the author. Nothing has been inferred: the thesis title, the
# author's full legal name, the institution, the supervisor and the ORCID appear
# NOWHERE in this repository, so none of them is written here.
#
# Before this file is used:
#   1. fill in the five placeholders below (search for "AUTHOR TO SUPPLY");
#   2. settle the licence question in the note at the bottom;
#   3. validate it — e.g. `cffconvert --validate` (pip install cffconvert), or
#      simply push and let GitHub's "Cite this repository" widget parse it. This
#      file was written without a validator available in the environment, and the
#      author-name keys in particular depend on how the placeholders are filled.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below. Please also
  cite the upstream work it builds on: CLAM (Lu et al.), the UNI/UNI2-h encoder
  (Chen et al.), TCGA-BRCA, CPTAC-BRCA and cBioPortal.
type: software

title: >-
  dp-code — PAM50 molecular-subtype classification from H&E whole-slide images
  fused with arm-level copy-number variation (TCGA-BRCA to CPTAC-BRCA)

abstract: >-
  Four-class PAM50 subtype classification (Luminal A, Luminal B, Basal-like,
  HER2-enriched) from H&E whole-slide images, trained on TCGA-BRCA with 10-fold
  patient-level cross-validation and externally validated on CPTAC-BRCA. The
  imaging arm is UNI2-h patch features with CLAM-MB attention-based multiple
  instance learning; the second modality is 39 chromosome-arm copy-number
  features. The repository reports the copy-number-alone arm and the untrained
  equal-weight probability mean alongside every fusion result, and finds that no
  trained fusion operator beats that mean.

authors:
