  # Neither the legal name, the institution nor an ORCID is recorded anywhere in
  # this repository, so none of them is guessed here.
  - alias: peterhubina
    email: peter.hubina1@gmail.com

repository-code: https://github.com/peterhubina/dp-code
version: 0.1.0

# Date of the most recent commit at the time this file was written. Update it, or
# drop it in favour of a tagged release date.
date-released: '2026-08-05'

keywords:
  - computational pathology
  - breast cancer
  - PAM50
  - molecular subtyping
  - multiple instance learning
  - multimodal fusion
  - copy-number variation
  - external validation
  - TCGA-BRCA
  - CPTAC-BRCA

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NO `license:` FIELD, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE.
#
# The licensing status of this repository is unresolved, and resolving it is an
# author-and-supervisor decision, not a documentation task:
#
#   * the root `LICENCE` is the unmodified Apache-2.0 text with its
#     `Copyright [yyyy] [name of copyright owner]` placeholder never filled;
#   * the only thing that ever filled that role was a line in the old root
#     `README.md`, which named the authors of the HistologyHSI-BC *dataset* --
#     so as published, the licence attributed this repository's code to someone
#     else. That notice now lives at `docs/parked-cohorts/histology-hsi-bc.md`,
#     where it belongs, which removes the confusion but not the question;
#   * `project/CLAM` and `project/MCAT` are GPLv3, and CLAM is modified in place
#     (`models/model_multimodal.py`, `multimodal_dataset.py`, the `--fusion_mode`
#     machinery). That makes the combined work a GPLv3 derivative, which is
#     inconsistent with distributing the whole repository under Apache-2.0. The
#     `topk` dependency is GPL as well.
#
# Declaring a `license:` here would assert a resolution nobody has made. Until
# the author decides, do not assume either licence applies to the combined work.
#
# AUTHOR TO SUPPLY: the licence decision, the filled copyright line in `LICENCE`,
# and (if the thesis is deposited) `doi:`, `preferred-citation:` and the
# institution/supervisor metadata for a `type: thesis` citation.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
